{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI (change 2235 ps1) failed: removing the class-name Mutation dispatch made typed dispatch class-identity-sensitive, so cross-loaded Mutation instances (the reconciler loads mutation.py under two sys.modules keys) fell through to the batch path -> AttributeError/'Mutation has no .get' + 'requires pass_id'. Root cause: bare isinstance(x, mut_mod.Mutation) binds one class identity. Fix (ps2): dispatch via an explicit @runtime_checkable declared protocol MutationShape (attributes direction+action) defined in apply_base.py and imported into applier.py -- identity-agnostic, no class-name string (AC4 poison holds), and exactly AC5's 'explicit declared protocol'. A batch dict lacks those attributes so it still routes to the batch path. Validated: census 9 passed; full tests/unit/rebar_reconciler 3579 passed/1 skipped; make lint + make typecheck green; applier 793 LOC (<800)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787729846142795001,"uuid":"e8136ed3-850e-477f-a625-2bf1fe0f000b"}